<h1>Omni Listings</h1>

The print version of Omni was a bedsheet-sized publication
started by Bob Guccione as a kind of sister magazine to
<i>Penthouse</i>. Omni always had a dual personality
with respect to its prestige.  On the one hand its high 
circulation, coupled with some outstanding fiction editors, 
allowed it to attract the cream of the crop in the speculative
fiction field. On the other hand, it's concentration on UFOs and
the paranormal gave it a reputation as being fairly eccentric.
<p>
The print version of Omni has been officially put to rest, with
its last issue being the Winter 1995 issue.
